  "term": "Seckel syndrome",
  "definition": "Seckel syndrome is a rare inherited condition passed in an autosomal recessive pattern. It is marked by severe growth restriction before birth, short stature, a very small head size, cognitive impairment, and a distinctive bird-like facial appearance.",
